    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d25">

                <pb facs="0164" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/543.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-09-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Viceroy at Chengtu has arrested the ringleaders and his ya-men has been
                    attacked by a mob. The soldiers fired and killed some twenty rioters; some
                    soldiers were killed also. American ladies and children are reported to have
                    left Chengtu, with the British subjects. Troops are being concentrated on the
                    frontier of Szechwan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
